>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_fmap_display`

``` hol4
Refute.register_fmap_display : unit -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Restores or refreshes Refute's built-in finite-map display
postprocessor.

The model finder's synthetic `fmap` typedef represents a value as
`key -> range option`, so a reconstructed `abs_fmap'` atom displays
through the same update-chain parser as any other function value.  This
registration rewrites that reconstructed representation into an
`FUPDATE` chain on `FEMPTY`, valid at every `:'a |-> 'b` instance.  A
base that is not literally `NONE` or an irrelevant-marker hole, or any
point whose value is itself an opaque marker, declines the rewrite
rather than guessing and leaves the raw term unchanged.

It is display-only, applied through the same walk
`Refute.register_term_postprocessor` installs into, after
`Refute.register_function_display`'s deduplication has already run on
the underlying representation.  A `register_term_postprocessor`
registration at exactly `:'a |-> 'b` replaces this built-in, since
registration matches on the pattern; this idempotent entry point
restores it afterward.  It is installed when `Refute` is loaded and
creates no HOL objects.

### See also

[`Refute.register_function_display`](#Refute.register_function_display),
[`Refute.register_term_postprocessor`](#Refute.register_term_postprocessor),
[`Refute.register_generator_family`](#Refute.register_generator_family),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Model reconstruction is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
